---
description: <What this rule enforces, in one line.>
alwaysApply: false
globs:
  - "<glob this rule applies to>"
---

<!--
Template for a new rule.

A rule answers "what applies to everyone doing this kind of work".
An agent answers "what is my role". Do not put role-specific instructions in a rule.

Frontmatter:
  description   required. One line; used for relevance matching when alwaysApply is false.
  alwaysApply   true  -> injected into every agent's context. Reserve for non-negotiables.
                false -> activated by description relevance or by `globs`.
  globs         optional list of file patterns that trigger the rule.

Guidance:
  * Keep agent-specific duties in the agent file. A rule duplicated into an agent drifts.
  * State the rule, then the reason briefly. Rules without reasons get worked around.
  * Use "Never" for hard prohibitions and "Prefer" for genuine trade-offs. Do not blur them.
  * If a rule can be checked mechanically, add the check to .agent/tools/validate.py instead —
    an executable invariant beats a written one.
-->

# <Rule title>

## <Section>

- ...
- ...

## Never

- ...
